and, so it falls short again and again.\n  - Candidate 5 orders about 1.2 times the forecast. The extra builds up, and some of product 0 expires and is written off.\n  - Candidate 3 orders about 1.09 times the forecast: a small surplus that acts as a buffer without much spoilage.\n- **Warehouse capacity (172 units).**\n  - Candidate 4 receives 170 units on day 9 on top of leftover stock, so part of that delivery would be lost.\n  - Candidate 6 receives 164 units on day 8, which with any leftover is at or over the limit. Its order sizes are also uneven, with some well below demand: on day 3 it orders 72 of product 1 against about 78 of forecast demand.\n  - Candidate 3's largest delivery is 131 units on day 9, which leaves comfortable room.\n\nOrdering every 2 or 3 days is about equal on cost, and pooling several days' demand evens out randomness for both. Candidate 3 combines one of the cheapest schedules with a reasonable size of order and no risk of overflowing the warehouse."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 353, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5786, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 353}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T08:09:27.398Z", "request_id": "req_011CgF3LfSTDYpUAjHuNiRhF"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LJ3ZgY6NhnDNgwqXm7qmvJ", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011C